  <prompt>
    Implement FR-26 (imported anchors survive save). Prove — through the wire — that imported revisions
    (task 050) and imported comments (task 051) anchor by `w14:paraId` (E2) and are PRESERVED across the
    retained-original delta save (E1, task 022): open a `.docx` that already has Word revisions/comments →
    save → reopen, and the imported revisions/comments are still present, still anchored to the correct
    paragraphs by paraId. The load-bearing deliverable is a **through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam
    slice test** in `tests/integration/seam/**` (per NFR-06 E2E Definition-of-Done + ADR-038) that drives
    Load → (edit elsewhere) → Save → Load and asserts the imported marks survive with correct paraId anchors.
    Any small production glue needed to make imported marks ride the E1 retained-original splice cleanly is in
    scope, but the primary work is the seam test. This is TEST-MODIFYING (modifies `tests/**`) → code-review +
    adr-check run at Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONALLY.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior test engineer fluent in `WebApplicationFactory` through-the-wire slice tests (ADR-038 KEEP
    categories, the `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam category), the Spaarke Compose
    Load/Save round-trip, Open XML revision/comment assertion, and the E1 retained-original delta save +
    E2 paraId substrate. Comfortable asserting a persisted OOXML side-effect (imported marks survive with
    correct paraId anchors) rather than a service-level unit.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `tests/integration/seam/**` `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test that: (1) Loads a fixture `.docx`
    carrying pre-existing Word `w:ins`/`w:del` + `w:comment`; (2) makes a dirty edit to an UNRELATED
    paragraph; (3) Saves through the real route (E1 retained-original delta); (4) reopens via Load; and
    asserts the imported revisions AND comments are still present, still anchored to their original
    paragraphs by `w14:paraId`, and NOT dropped or re-flattened. Plus any minimal production glue so
    imported marks ride the E1 splice cleanly. code-review + adr-check pass at Step 9.5 (TEST-MODIFYING
    override). The BFF build + the new seam test are green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-26 is the import round-trip's survival guarantee: imported revisions/comments anchor by paraId
      (E2) and must be preserved across the retained-original save (E1). Design §7 attaches imported marks
      "by paraId so they survive the retained-original save — the same substrate the fidelity core builds."
      Tasks 050/051 wire the reader into Load and render the marks; this task proves they survive the
      round-trip and adds the through-the-wire seam test. Per the R3 CLAUDE.md E2E Definition-of-Done
      (NFR-06): every save/load/dispatch change carries a `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test in
      `tests/integration/seam/**`; unit-green ≠ done; `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`/DI-registration/ctor-null
      tests do NOT satisfy (ADR-038).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/ — NEW `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test: Load(redlined+commented docx) → edit unrelated para → Save (E1 delta) → Load → assert imported revisions + comments survive with correct paraId anchors (NFR-06, ADR-038 seam category)</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — `LoadAsync` (`:168`, imported-mark projection from tasks 050/051) + `SaveAsync` (E1 retained-original delta, task 022) — the round-trip under test</file>
      <file role="canonical-reuse">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs — `Read(byte[])` (`:68`) used to assert imported marks are present after reopen</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/tasks/024-*.poml — the FR-07/NFR-06 fidelity seam slice test (task 024) is the reference shape for a through-the-wire compose seam test; mirror its `WebApplicationFactory` harness</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §7 (imported marks anchor by paraId, survive save), §8 (SAVE dirty pipeline), §12 (test obligation — through-the-wire slice)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="022" status="pending">FR-01 E1 cutover (retained-original baseline in `SaveAsync`) — the save path the imported marks must survive.</dependency>
      <dependency task="050" status="pending">FR-24 import existing revisions — the imported revisions under test.</dependency>
      <dependency task="051" status="pending">FR-25 import existing comments — the imported comments under test.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 / NFR-06">The DoD deliverable MUST be a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test in `tests/integration/seam/**` that POSTs through the REAL Save route and asserts the persisted OOXML side-effect (imported marks survive with correct paraId). `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration tests, and ctor-null tests are BANNED and do NOT satisfy this. Unit-green ≠ done.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / MUST anchor by paraId">The test MUST assert imported marks resolve by `w14:paraId` after the round-trip; the fuzzy `AnnotationReanchorService` fallback is a secondary path, not the primary assertion.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project / FR-01 MUST">The save under test MUST derive from the retained load-time original (E1); the test asserts untouched content (incl. the imported marks on untouched paragraphs) is preserved and the dirty edit lands on exactly its paragraph.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">The seam test exercises the real facade path; no `Microsoft.Graph` type is asserted above `SpeFileStore`. Fixtures + assertions operate on `byte[]`/OOXML.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` stays AI-facade-clean; any production glue added here injects no AI internals (Tier-1 NetArchTest green).</constraint>
    <constraint source="TEST-MODIFYING override / CLAUDE.md §8">This task modifies `tests/**` → code-review + adr-check run at Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONALLY (overrides any default skip).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 / §10 BFF hygiene">Report publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (test-only + minor glue → ≈0; state it); verify no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

