  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Declare rigor (FULL, TEST-MODIFYING). Confirm deps 022 (E1 cutover), 050 (import revisions), 051 (import comments) are ✅. Load ADR-038 + TEST-ARCHITECTURE + the seam-category KEEP rule. Read task 024's seam-test shape as the reference harness.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Build the fixture">Create/obtain a `.docx` fixture that already carries Word `w:ins`/`w:del` + a `w:comment` thread on known paragraphs (with paraIds). Keep it small and deterministic.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Author the seam slice test">In `tests/integration/seam/**`, author a `WebApplicationFactory` test: Load the fixture → assert imported marks present on load (from tasks 050/051) → make a dirty edit to an UNRELATED paragraph → Save through the REAL Save route (E1 delta) → reopen via Load.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Assert survival + paraId anchoring">Assert the imported revisions AND comments are still present after reopen, anchored to their original paragraphs by `w14:paraId`, NOT dropped or re-flattened; assert the unrelated dirty edit landed on exactly its paragraph and untouched content (incl. imported marks) is preserved (FR-26 + FR-01).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Minimal production glue (if needed)">If the round-trip reveals imported marks do not ride the E1 splice cleanly, add the minimal `Services/Compose/` glue to fix it (no AI internals; paraId-anchored). Keep the change bounded; the primary deliverable is the seam test.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Verify + gates">Build BFF; run the seam test (green). Run the NetArchTest facade check. Run code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 (unconditional — TEST-MODIFYING). Report publish-size delta (~0) + CVE. Update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/ — imported-marks-survive-save WebApplicationFactory seam slice test</output>
