    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ (minimal glue only if the round-trip requires it)</output>
    <output type="report">Seam-test evidence (imported marks survive with paraId anchors); publish-size delta; CVE; code-review + adr-check result</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test in `tests/integration/seam/**` drives Load(redlined+commented docx) → dirty edit to an unrelated paragraph → Save through the REAL route (E1 delta) → Load, and asserts the imported revisions AND comments survive (FR-26 acceptance: open→save→reopen preserves them).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test asserts imported marks resolve by `w14:paraId` to their original paragraphs after the round-trip (E2), not by fuzzy fallback as the primary path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test asserts untouched content (incl. imported marks on untouched paragraphs) is preserved and the dirty edit landed on exactly its paragraph (FR-01/E1).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test crosses the HTTP boundary through the real Save route; NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor-null test is used (ADR-038); it lives at the `tests/integration/seam/**` KEEP path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Any production glue added injects no AI internals (NetArchTest green) and no `Microsoft.Graph` type in `Services/Compose/` (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">code-review + adr-check run at Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONALLY (TEST-MODIFYING) and are clean or carry documented Path-A/B resolutions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size reported delta vs ~49.63 MB (≈0; test-only + minor glue); no new HIGH CVE; BFF build + seam test green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

